In this entrepreneurship project, we worked as aspiring entrepreneurs with an innovative idea aimed at building a startup and scaling it into a successful venture. Our project, *Yusr*, is a smart Hajj wristband designed to enhance pilgrims’ experience through the following key features:

• AI-based automatic counting of Tawaf and Sa’i rounds
• Continuous health monitoring with real-time alerts
• SOS emergency system with live location sharing
• Direct voice communication via the wristband
• Companion mobile app for guidance, supplications, and navigation
• Real-time location tracking within holy sites
• Communication center for receiving important updates
• Detailed gate maps for easy navigation

Throughout the project, we went through six main entrepreneurial phases:

1. Market Research: Identifying target customers, analyzing needs, and studying competitors
2. MVP Development: Creating a minimum viable product through a demo video and a landing page showcasing the solution
3. Business Modeling: Developing the Business Model Canvas and Lean Canvas
4. Marketing Phase: Promoting the project and reaching a wide audience, achieving strong engagement
5. Financial Planning: Analyzing cost structure, revenue streams, funding needs, and profitability timeline
6. Final Report: Delivering a comprehensive report covering all aspects of *Yusr* and its market potential

This project reflects a complete entrepreneurial journey from idea validation to market and financial analysis.

